MeiHigekiri: {
	DisplayName: Higekiri
	Origin: The night of the test cut, the head fell with the beard still clinging to the edge — hence the old name
	Power: Beard-Cutter: Zanshin and the World-Razing Flash deal escalating finisher damage to targets below 35% life (up to +50%, +25% vs bosses); finishing a target with either art refunds 10 stance, once per strike
	Burden: Weapon damage -10% — against the healthy, this blade bites duller than the original name
	Summary: Stronger finishers on low-life targets, kills refund stance; weapon damage -10%
}

MeiOnikiri: {
	DisplayName: Onikiri
	Origin: At Ichijo-Modoribashi, the oni that lost its arm never dared come back for it. The name has been nailed to the tang ever since
	Power: The original inscription. The blade stays exactly as it is — nothing granted, nothing taken
	Burden: ———
	Summary: Original inscription: keeps the blade as-is, no boon, no price
}

MeiShishinoko: {
	DisplayName: Shishi-no-ko
	Origin: Left by the pillow at midnight, the blade roared like a lion. Inlaid in gold, to honor the name
	Power: Lion's Roar: complete five combo beats without dash or art interruption and the fifth beat roars — two converging jaw-waves (about 40% of a slash in total)
	Burden: Combo beat interval +10% — a roar must be drawn in before it is let out
	Summary: Jaw-waves crown a full five-beat combo; combo 10% slower
}

MeiTomokiri: {
	DisplayName: Tomokiri
	Origin: Crossed with a friendly blade in trial, it cut the friend in two. A name of blame, chiseled into the tang; the sword has run violent since
	Power: Friend-Cutter: cancelling a combo with the Kamui flash step leaves a delayed phantom slash (about 35% power) that bites shut after a beat
	Burden: Damage taken +10% while held; each phantom adds a layer of Guilt (max 3), each making the next flash step cost 6 more vigor — repaid on a Zanshin hit
	Summary: Dash-cancels leave phantom slashes; +10% damage taken, Guilt taxes dashes
}

MeiKazehi: {
	DisplayName: Kaze-hi
	Origin: A groove opened like a wind channel; where the blade passes, only wind is heard, no blade is seen
	Power: Wind-Rider: flash step vigor cost -25%, sakura flight drain -30%
	Burden: Flash mark damage -25% — the groove was cut for lightness, not slaughter
	Summary: Cheaper footwork and flight; flash mark damage -25%
}

MeiChihi: {
	DisplayName: Chi-hi
	Origin: This groove is not for lightness, but for letting blood — so said the one who opened the edge
	Power: Bloodletting: the first combo hit of each beat restores +2 extra vigor, a Zanshin hit restores +8
	Burden: Natural vigor regen halved, regen delay +0.4s after spending — no blood on the edge, no breath returned
	Summary: Stronger on-hit vigor; natural regen halved
}

MeiFudo: {
	DisplayName: Fudo
	Origin: Carved in the brushwork of the seed syllable Kan — the Immovable One sits by the edge, flames at his back
	Power: Immovable: when struck during heavy combo beats, Zanshin or executions, spend 20 stance to cut that blow's damage by 40% and ignore its knockback (about 2s cooldown); the dismemberment backlash is never shielded
	Burden: Stance gain -20% — the guarding strength is skimmed from your build-up
	Summary: Spend stance to stand through committed strikes; stance gain -20%
}

MeiKurikara: {
	DisplayName: Kurikara
	Origin: The dragon coils about the sword and would swallow it — an old horimono subject, its scales inlaid in gold
	Power: Dragon-Coil: after the World-Razing Flash or the Finale, the carving ignites; finish a five-beat combo within ten seconds and the fifth beat looses a coiling dragonfire slash (about 40% power)
	Burden: Vigor cap 100 → 80 — where the dragon coils, breath cannot pass
	Summary: Executions ignite a dragonfire follow-up combo; vigor cap -20
}

MeiTessetsu: {
	DisplayName: Tessetsu
	Origin: A grand name for a scrap of iron — nailed into the tang as a joke that stuck
	Power: Iron-Cut: Zanshin and the World-Razing Flash deal escalating finisher damage on low-life targets; the blade is duller overall
	Burden: Weapon damage -15% — strong on leftovers, clumsy on full health
	Summary: Low-life execute; damage -15%
}

MeiKyushu: {
	DisplayName: Kyushu
	Origin: The head is still the old one. Cut clean; no need for a scare-name
	Power: Old-Head: Zanshin and the World-Razing Flash deal escalating finisher damage on low-life targets
	Burden: Weapon damage -8% — old method, lighter tax
	Summary: Low-life execute; damage -8%
}

MeiIkiai: {
	DisplayName: Ikiai
	Origin: The breath you held while staring — then the blades met on the beat
	Power: Breath-Match: finish an uninterrupted combo for a closing jaw wave
	Burden: Combo beat interval +5% — shallow charge, not gold renown
	Summary: Combo jaw wave; slightly slower combo
}

MeiKyoko: {
	DisplayName: Kyoko
	Origin: A roar into empty air; the echo finds no place to land
	Power: Hollow-Roar: finish an uninterrupted combo for a closing jaw wave
	Burden: Combo beat interval +14% — slower when focus breaks
	Summary: Combo jaw wave; slower combo
}

MeiKarikiri: {
	DisplayName: Karikiri
	Origin: Learned so well it turned fake. A guilt-shadow step enters the tang
	Power: False-Cut: cancelling a combo with the flash step leaves a delayed echo cut
	Burden: Damage taken +12% while held; Guilt stacks tax dash vigor
	Summary: Dash-cancel echo; incoming +12%
}

MeiMokukiri: {
	DisplayName: Mokukiri
	Origin: The air sank. You got used to it. The guilt stayed
	Power: Quiet-Cut: cancelling a combo with the flash step leaves a delayed echo cut
	Burden: Damage taken +8% while held; Guilt stacks tax dash vigor
	Summary: Dash-cancel echo; incoming +8%
}

MeiKogehi: {
	DisplayName: Koge-hi
	Origin: Do not put your foot in the hot shallows. The groove is for stepping clear
	Power: Scorch-Groove: cheaper dash vigor; sakura drain slightly cheaper
	Burden: Flash mark damage lower — standing still hurts more
	Summary: Cheaper movement; weaker flash marks
}

MeiKanhi: {
	DisplayName: Kan-hi
	Origin: Quiet by the door. Let the ears rest
	Power: Idle-Groove: cheaper sakura cruise; dash slightly cheaper
	Burden: Flash mark damage slightly lower — idle travel, not hard trades
	Summary: Cheaper cruise; slightly weaker marks
}

MeiTodohi: {
	DisplayName: Todo-hi
	Origin: A bit sticky. Keep contact to turn; break off and it stalls
	Power: Sticking-Groove: combo hits restore a bit more vigor
	Burden: Worse natural regen and longer post-skill delay — drought out of contact
	Summary: Contact regen; worse out-of-fight regen
}

MeiShiorihi: {
	DisplayName: Shiori-hi
	Origin: Cut the spent flower to open the edge — not for looks
	Power: Wither-Groove: stronger Zanshin vigor return; lighter combo return
	Burden: Natural regen still poor — empty swings do not feed the blade
	Summary: Stronger Zanshin regen; poor natural regen
}

MeiShiohi: {
	DisplayName: Shio-hi
	Origin: Tide marks overnight. Wet contact feeds the return
	Power: Tide-Groove: hit and Zanshin vigor stretch longer
	Burden: Worse natural regen — overnight drought when you disengage
	Summary: Wet-contact regen; worse disengage regen
}

MeiShibori: {
	DisplayName: Shibori
	Origin: Guard even with numb hands. The blade hurts too
	Power: Numb-Carving: spend stance to blunt hits during committed moves
	Burden: Stance gain -30% — thicker guard costs more poise
	Summary: Commit-window guard; stance gain -30%
}

MeiChinmei: {
	DisplayName: Chinmei
	Origin: When the ears buzz, settle first, then move
	Power: Still-Ring: spend stance to blunt hits during committed moves
	Burden: Stance gain -15% — rest-guard; aggressive builds stack slower
	Summary: Commit-window guard; stance gain -15%
}

MeiAshidome: {
	DisplayName: Ashidome
	Origin: Stand still. Guard lives where the feet stop
	Power: Planted-Feet: spend stance to blunt hits during committed moves
	Burden: Stance gain -22% — running while cutting still feels unprotected
	Summary: Commit-window guard; stance gain -22%
}

MeiYoen: {
	DisplayName: Yoen
	Origin: Oven heat still on the edge. Fire out; burn not gone
	Power: Ember-Remnant: after an execution, a full combo last beat looses a dragonfire ring
	Burden: Slightly lower vigor cap — embers can still empty the tank
	Summary: Post-execute dragonfire combo; slightly lower vigor cap
}
